      ":question/problem": "The population of a city is given by the function $n(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in years, from when records first began. The values of $n(t)$, in thousands, for different values of $t$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $n(t)$ | $851$ | $856$ | $861$ | $865$ | $870$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of growth in population in the second year $(t = 2)$ using a forward difference approximation.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
