      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-71925",
      ":question/problem": "The total number of eggs laid by a pen of chickens on a farm is given by the function $e(t),$ where $t$ is the number of days since the chickens arrived on the farm. The values of $e(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $e(t)$ | $20$ | $45$ | $77$ | $117$ | $160$ | $195$ |\n\nApproximate the rate at which eggs are laid at the $4$th day using a forward difference approximation."
